{% extends '@layout/blog-post.html.twig' %}

{% block body %}
As all <a href="http://www.aptana.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">aptana</a> fans know, <a href="http://www.aptana.org/php" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Aptana PHP</a> plugin was discontinued in Aptana 2.x, in favor of PDT.
 But PDT is a joke, not suitable for professional PHP development, major features are missing.
 So if you want to continue using Aptana PHP, that's what need to be done:
<ol>
    <li>Aptana -> Help -> Install New Software</li>
    <li>Add http://update.aptana.com/install/php</li>
    <li>Then select Aptana PHP and install it.</li>
</ol>

In case you don't have yet a SVN plugin, go to
<ol>
    <li>Aptana -> Help -> Install Aptana Features</li>
    <li>Others -> Subclipse</li>
    <li>Follow the instructions</li>
</ol>
{% endblock %}
